Hi.

Let me present you a Gehennom branch I've worked on.

It's called Sheol after the Hebrew Bible's underworld.

The idea of this branch is to introduce something different (and 
challenging) to all those boring mazes in Gehennom. Sheol has a brand new 
level generator, new hand-made levels, new monsters with unique abilities 
(some only appearing in Sheol), new wall types and a new item.

Sheol is icy cold in contrast to fiery hell of Gehennom.

Sheol is designed to be dangerous even for late game characters. You most 
likely will want levitation and wands of fire to melt ice. Wands of fire 
have much higher chance of appearing on Sheol levels.

Vlad's tower is now in Sheol.

In addition, there is relevant (I hope) loot to be pillaged in Sheol, 
such as a guaranteed magic marker and a magic lamp. An optional boss-like 
monster is also present (called the Executioner).

It breaks save compatibility, bones compatibility, possibly tiles 
compatibility (I don't know how they work) and maybe several other 
compatibilities I didn't even think of.

I only updated the unix Makefiles to know about Sheol files.

Here's a screenshot of a typical Sheol level (pardon the non-ideal font 
choice for DECgraphics):
http://i.imgur.com/BmgeQ.png

The white and cyan walls are icy walls than can be melted with a wand of 
fire or other fire sources.

The code for this mod is on github, at here:
https://github.com/Noeda/nethack-sheol

Also read the Very Official Documentation on Sheol (it's under doc/
sheol.txt in the sources but you can view it online here):
https://github.com/Noeda/nethack-sheol/blob/master/doc/sheol.txt

